      "hypotheses": "In the unitary lattice setting, n≥1, the real Witt index is at most q at every place, and the least normalized size τ is below 1/2. The canonical flag and its size and isotropy properties are used.",
      "statement": "The ratios of the a≤q consecutive sizes up to 1/2 multiply to 2τ. Thus a nonzero saturated isotropic R has upper size h and lower quotient size l with h/l≤u and h²≤u/4, where u=(2τ)^(1/q).",
