      "hypotheses": "At level g≥1, use the two lattice covering radii for R and its central maps, the canonical rational Hermitian frame, and strong approximation for the unitary unipotent radical.",
      "statement": "Rounding first modulo the center at scale 2g, then inside the center at scale g after the commutator correction, writes the real orbit element as a rational unipotent translate of a representative of radius ≤n²√f g d u/4 up to finite level. Functions invariant on the left by rational elements and on the right by this level have the same values throughout the adelic orbit as at these representatives.",
